  "summary_en": "Book chapter surveying normative problems of increasingly autonomous robotic systems to draw lessons for AI in judicial proceedings. Using autonomous weapons and surgical robots as case studies, it examines acceptability of autonomous decision-making in sensitive domains and human responsibility for harm, applying these to shared human-software control in judging.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Autonomous weapons illustrate whether autonomous decision-making is acceptable in ethically and legally sensitive domains.",
